# Every file already in this repository is stored with CRLF, and the only
# consumers are Windows: the server, the deployment scripts, the SQL that
# sqlcmd runs. `-text` therefore means "store exactly what is on disk" — no
# end-of-line conversion in either direction.
#
# The alternative, `* text=auto`, is the usual advice and is wrong here: with
# the history already CRLF it would renormalise every file to LF the next time
# it is touched, turning a one-line fix into a whole-file diff. It would also
# quietly make new commits disagree with old ones about line endings, which is
# what `core.autocrlf=true` was about to do to server/src/lib/errors.js.
* -text
